---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  CalendarCaptions,
  CalendarDatePicker,
  CalendarLayouts,
  CalendarPlayground,
  CalendarSelection,
} from "../../components/CalendarDemo";
---

<Docs
  title="Calendar"
  description="A month grid for picking one date, several dates, or a range."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Calendar</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A month grid for picking one date, several dates, or a range. Use it on its
    own in a form, or inside a popover as a date picker.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="calendar-demo"><CalendarPlayground client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Calendar usage"
      code={`import { useState } from "react";
import { Calendar } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/calendar";

const [date, setDate] = useState<Date | undefined>(new Date(2026, 9, 12));

<Calendar
  mode="single"
  selected={date}
  onSelect={setDate}
  defaultMonth={new Date(2026, 9, 1)}
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>Calendar</code> wraps <a href="https://daypicker.dev"
        >React DayPicker</a
      > 10 and takes all of its props. Sprõut adds its own styles, Sprõut buttons
      for month navigation, and Sprõut selects for the month and year menus.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="calendar-selection">
    <h2 class="section-title">Selection modes</h2>
    <p>
      Set <code>mode</code> to <code>"single"</code>, <code>"range"</code>, or <code
        >"multiple"</code
      >, and control the value with <code>selected</code> and <code
        >onSelect</code
      >. A range passes <code>{"{ from, to }"}</code>; the first and last days
      are filled and the days between share a band. Pass a matcher to <code
        >disabled</code
      >, such as <code>{"{ dayOfWeek: [0, 6] }"}</code> for weekends.
    </p>
    <CalendarSelection client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="calendar-captions">
    <h2 class="section-title">Captions and navigation</h2>
    <p>
      <code>captionLayout="label"</code> (default) shows the month name. <code
        >"dropdown"</code
      > shows month and year menus; <code>"dropdown-months"</code> and <code
        >"dropdown-years"</code
      > show one. <code>buttonVariant</code> picks the <code>Button</code> variant
      for the previous and next buttons: <code>"ghost"</code> (default) or <code
        >"outline"</code
      >.
    </p>
    <CalendarCaptions client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="calendar-date-picker">
    <h2 class="section-title">Date picker</h2>
    <p>
      Put the calendar straight inside <code>PopoverContent</code>. It fills the
      panel and drops its own surface. Close the popover in <code>onSelect</code
      > and ignore <code>undefined</code> so clicking the chosen day again doesn’t
      clear it.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Calendar date picker"
      code={`<Popover open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen}>
  <h2 aria-label={title}>
    <PopoverTrigger
      render={<Button variant="ghost" size="calendar-title" aria-label="Choose date" />}
    >
      {title}
      <ChevronDown size={14} aria-hidden="true" />
    </PopoverTrigger>
  </h2>
  <PopoverContent align="start" aria-label="Choose a calendar date">
    <Calendar
      mode="single"
      weekStartsOn={1}
      selected={day}
      defaultMonth={day}
      onSelect={(date) => {
        if (date) {
          setOpen(false);
          show(date);
        }
      }}
    />
  </PopoverContent>
</Popover>`}
    />
    <CalendarDatePicker client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="calendar-layouts">
    <h2 class="section-title">Layout and custom days</h2>
    <p>
      <code>numberOfMonths</code> shows months side by side from 768px and stacked
      below. <code>showWeekNumber</code> adds a week column, and <code
        >weekStartsOn</code
      > sets the first weekday. To add content under a date, render <code
        >CalendarDayButton</code
      > from <code>components.DayButton</code> and put the extra content in a <code
        >span</code
      >. Set <code>--sprout-calendar-cell</code> to make room.
    </p>
    <CalendarLayouts client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="calendar-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>Calendar</code> takes every React DayPicker prop. Sprõut sets <code
        >showOutsideDays</code
      > to <code>true</code> and <code>captionLayout</code> to <code
        >"label"</code
      >, and adds <code>buttonVariant</code> (<code>"ghost"</code>). Your <code
        >classNames</code
      >, <code>formatters</code>, and <code>components</code> merge over Sprõut’s.
      The root has <code>data-slot="calendar"</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>CalendarDayButton</code> is the day button. It takes the DayPicker day
      button props and sets <code>data-selected-single</code>, <code
        >data-range-start</code
      >, <code>data-range-middle</code>, <code>data-range-end</code>, and <code
        >data-day</code
      >. The package also exports the <code>DateRange</code> and <code
        >Matcher</code
      > types.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The month is a labelled grid. Tab moves to the selected day, or today.
      Arrow keys move by day and week, Home and End go to the start and end of
      the week, Page Up and Page Down change month, and Shift with Page Up or
      Page Down changes year. Enter or Space selects. Disabled days stay
      readable but can’t be chosen.
    </p>
    <p>
      Day colors change over 120ms, with no motion when reduced motion is
      requested. In forced-colors mode selected days keep an outline.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Selected days use <code>--sprout-primary</code> and <code
        >--sprout-on-primary</code
      >, so they follow the TulipFarm brand when you opt in. Today and range
      bands use <code>--sprout-hover</code>; muted text uses <code
        >--sprout-muted</code
      >. Set <code>--sprout-calendar-cell</code> (1.75rem) and <code
        >--sprout-calendar-radius</code
      > on the calendar to resize it.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
